    "Which color of sunlight scatters more and makes the daytime sky look blue?": "/audio/unified/voice_1246afecdc6a3b9a.mp3",
    "Which star is closest to Earth?": "/audio/unified/voice_9b974b3e70347d19.mp3",
    "What lights up the Moon?": "/audio/unified/voice_a8341e185b99d3b9.mp3",
    "What makes day turn into night?": "/audio/unified/voice_c6409ed64f68b9a9.mp3",
    "Which part of a plant takes in water from the soil?": "/audio/unified/voice_37cda617c3375b9a.mp3",
    "What are most clouds made of?": "/audio/unified/voice_0922f78e1ce26ca8.mp3",
    "What does water become when it freezes?": "/audio/unified/voice_90b81693967ff28e.mp3",
    "What helps a green plant make its food?": "/audio/unified/voice_ff5edd5a1919fcb7.mp3",
    "What carries most sounds from across a room to your ears?": "/audio/unified/voice_7f15ff2a4bc7cc16.mp3",
    "What do we call a sound that bounces back to us?": "/audio/unified/voice_2a2eb85027e142d9.mp3",
    "What pumps blood around your body?": "/audio/unified/voice_b5392f62113b434d.mp3",
    "What helps a fish get oxygen from water?": "/audio/unified/voice_b0aee4912dd6859e.mp3",
    "What can a caterpillar grow into?": "/audio/unified/voice_bca5aed2e60a0812.mp3",
    "What does a bird move to push air down and fly?": "/audio/unified/voice_eac8c9a440fb509f.mp3",
    "Where does water from a drying puddle go?": "/audio/unified/voice_f4892c519ae7bf2d.mp3",
    "What pulls a dropped ball toward Earth?": "/audio/unified/voice_2c2fd3add3e42cd6.mp3",
    "Sunlight has many colors, like a rainbow. Tiny bits of air scatter blue light in all directions, so the sky looks blue.": "/audio/unified/voice_808957d772415aff.mp3",
    "Grass has a green helper called chlorophyll that catches sunlight. Think of each blade as a little solar panel that helps the grass make food.": "/audio/unified/voice_53baacb915c1e217.mp3",
    "Sleep gives your body time to rest and your brain time to sort what you learned. It is a bit like putting your toys back in their boxes after playing.": "/audio/unified/voice_6133ce60d83b5d12.mp3",
    "Rivers carry tiny bits of salt from rocks into the sea. When water rises into the air, the salt stays behind, a little like salt left in a bowl after water dries.": "/audio/unified/voice_bddcaf12b22da1c2.mp3",
    "Clouds are full of tiny drops of water that bump together and grow. When they get heavy enough, they fall like drops from a wet sponge.": "/audio/unified/voice_27207c6baeb48f36.mp3",
    "Stars are huge balls of hot gas that make their own light. They look like tiny lights because most are very far away. The Sun is our closest star.": "/audio/unified/voice_4088884c4b8ab522.mp3",
    "The Moon shines because sunlight bounces off its surface. Think of it like a ball lit by a flashlight.": "/audio/unified/voice_e302bb35175e9a7e.mp3",
    "Earth spins like a top. When your part faces the Sun it is day, and when it turns away it is night.": "/audio/unified/voice_04c0580bd0257a02.mp3",
    "Plants use sunlight, air, and water to make food and grow. Their roots take in water like little drinking straws.": "/audio/unified/voice_02e6c2e9649e2ca1.mp3",
    "Clouds are made of tiny drops of water or bits of ice. A cloud is a little like fog floating high above the ground.": "/audio/unified/voice_e3cf049fecf4ced9.mp3",
    "When water gets cold enough, its tiny pieces slow down and lock together to make ice. Think of loose building blocks snapping into a solid shape.": "/audio/unified/voice_fab2fa6148a46799.mp3",
    "When sunlight passes through raindrops, the drops spread its colors out. Each drop is a bit like a tiny piece of shiny glass.": "/audio/unified/voice_3ac791f6ff38b949.mp3",
    "Dogs let heat out when they pant. Moving air over their wet tongues cools them a little, like a breeze on damp skin.": "/audio/unified/voice_2dd20db2b8c3342f.mp3",
    "A cat makes a purr by moving parts in its throat as it breathes. Cats often purr when relaxed, a little like a quiet motor.": "/audio/unified/voice_7402736cebec4e21.mp3",
    "Birds push air down with their wings, and the air pushes the birds up. You can think of their wings as paddles that push against the air.": "/audio/unified/voice_23429839ff570f19.mp3",
    "Fish pass water over their gills, which pick up oxygen from the water. Gills do a job a little like your lungs, but in water.": "/audio/unified/voice_6d07049b42af90bf.mp3",
    "Bees can make a buzz by moving their wings very fast. The quick movements shake the air, like a tiny drum beating very quickly.": "/audio/unified/voice_7a793a257220d30c.mp3",
    "A caterpillar changes inside a shell called a chrysalis. When that change is done, a butterfly comes out with wings.": "/audio/unified/voice_7d35bf26effc9e4c.mp3",
    "Your heart squeezes to push blood through your body. It works like a little pump that keeps moving while you work, play, or sleep.": "/audio/unified/voice_95794c733c11ffd6.mp3",
    "Your bones hold your body up and protect parts inside you. Together, they make a frame a bit like the beams that hold up a house.": "/audio/unified/voice_121324832ffdd0ad.mp3",
    "Sound makes the air wiggle, and those wiggles move a thin part inside your ear. Your ear and brain work together to tell you what made the sound.": "/audio/unified/voice_9c53f856ba78fe7c.mp3",
    "An echo happens when sound bounces off something and comes back to you. It is like rolling a ball toward a wall and watching it bounce back.": "/audio/unified/voice_c8ba5d4c516266d8.mp3",
    "A sneeze is a quick blast of air that can clear dust from your nose. It is like your nose’s own little cleaning puff.": "/audio/unified/voice_f9d5aeff22fdd6fc.mp3",
    "Lightning heats the air around it very quickly. That air pushes outward, making the loud sound we call thunder.": "/audio/unified/voice_4afb9b98befdf54d.mp3",
    "Snow starts as tiny bits of ice inside clouds. More ice sticks to them as they grow, like little building blocks making a pattern.": "/audio/unified/voice_a37e3a3ef3ea89f3.mp3",
    "Sunlight warms some places more than others. Air moves as warmer air rises, and that moving air is wind.": "/audio/unified/voice_4d781a43e9e5f432.mp3",
    "Water in a puddle can turn into a gas and mix with the air. That is why a puddle grows smaller like wet clothes drying on a line.": "/audio/unified/voice_ee1f7d3a6cf94d7a.mp3",
    "A candle flame gets its fuel from melted wax that moves up the wick. The wick is like a tiny straw that brings wax to the flame.": "/audio/unified/voice_99cdf34649336893.mp3",
    "Saturn’s rings are made of many pieces of ice and rock moving around the planet. From far away, those pieces look like wide, bright bands.": "/audio/unified/voice_2ee93125261759fd.mp3",
    "Gravity pulls things toward Earth. It is like an invisible tug that keeps your feet on the ground and brings a dropped ball back down.": "/audio/unified/voice_ca3bb7992b6430cb.mp3",
    "The hero wears a round green mask with two very big goggles.": "/audio/unified/voice_be36cd625e17d1bf.mp3",
    "Under the goggles there is a wide, happy smile.": "/audio/unified/voice_161a4db5538a4c25.mp3",
    "The suit is green, with a bright yellow stripe across the chest.": "/audio/unified/voice_2af0ab794fd44d01.mp3",
    "Each hand has four fingers, and every fingertip is a big round sticky dot.": "/audio/unified/voice_4069dffd3619dd02.mp3",
    "A short yellow cape flutters behind the hero.": "/audio/unified/voice_d281e4a7c749d8c6.mp3",
    "A long curly tail swings from the back, with a little star at the tip.": "/audio/unified/voice_e8e7eb266acae122.mp3",
    "Child. Children come in many heights, so this explorer is just one example.": "/audio/unified/voice_3557ae99fa02f821.mp3",
    "Blue whale. The biggest animal on Earth eats tiny creatures called krill.": "/audio/unified/voice_b4a5d9db707f5978.mp3",
    "Mount Everest. Everest's snowy peak is the highest spot above sea level on Earth.": "/audio/unified/voice_173a684de2800e20.mp3",
    "Moon. The Moon looks bright because it reflects light from the Sun.": "/audio/unified/voice_1e43c451c563e308.mp3",
    "Earth. Oceans cover most of Earth, giving our home its blue color from space.": "/audio/unified/voice_4f71cb60f6c4b9a9.mp3",
    "Jupiter. Jupiter's Great Red Spot is a giant storm.": "/audio/unified/voice_2cae80848e5f1442.mp3",
    "Sun. Sunlight takes about eight minutes to reach Earth.": "/audio/unified/voice_03f89d431000c501.mp3",
    "Betelgeuse. This reddish star is part of a group of stars we call Orion.": "/audio/unified/voice_c1b66badb14ab9c0.mp3",
    "Let us clap our hands together! Clap, clap, clap!": "/audio/unified/voice_279630fa56e0bedf.mp3",
    "Super clapping!": "/audio/unified/voice_f293f2b0d949a711.mp3",
